# Cropper instance

`CropperInstance<E>` is a structural type for `bind:this` and callback arguments. It is not a constructor. `FixedCropperInstance<E>` adds `FixedCropperSettings` to the extension. Use a `$state` binding and `$derived` reads:

<CodeBlock highlighted={source.highlighted} code={source.code} />

## Reading and changing state

Getters are reactive. Mutation methods and callbacks run untracked. Treat returned observations as read-only; change the crop through methods. A disabled cropper still accepts programmatic actions.

`reset()` rebuilds from defaults; `refresh()` measures and reconciles layout. Both are asynchronous. `setImage(image)` installs a plain displayed-image value without reloading or resetting coordinates. `setState` accepts a complete state, `null`, or an updater; it does not accept a partial state.

`setCoordinates` accepts partial coordinates, functions and sequential arrays. Each function sees the result of earlier transforms. Its extension-aware update type is:

```ts
type CoordinateUpdate<E extends SettingsExtension> =
	| Partial<Coordinates>
	| null
	| ((state: CropperState, settings: CropperSettings<E>) => Partial<Coordinates> | null);
```

`getCoordinates()` rounds by default; pass `{ round: false }` for fractional values. `getStencilCoordinates()` uses boundary pixels. `getTransforms()` returns identity transforms when empty.

## Operation options

The core option interfaces have optional boolean fields: `TransitionOptions.transitions`, `ImmediatelyOptions.immediately`, `InteractionOptions.interaction`, `NormalizeOptions.normalize` and `PostprocessOptions.postprocess`. Omitted options retain the core method's behavior. To perform an immediate edit without an animated transition, pass `{ transitions: false }`.

Gesture methods accept boundary-pixel deltas with normalization enabled. Pair `moveCoordinates`, `resizeCoordinates` and `transformImage` with their corresponding end methods for custom interactions. The `parameters` argument of `resizeCoordinates` is typed `unknown` by the core; built-in stencils supply `ResizeOptions`.

## Canvas lifetime

`getCanvas(options?: DrawOptions)` returns `null` before readiness, without a usable source, or when canvas export is disabled. The returned canvas is reused by later exports; copy or encode it before another export if you need a snapshot. Rotated-image scratch pixels are released after drawing. The application owns images and object URLs it passes to `setImage`.

## Methods

All 33 public methods are listed below. Optional option objects default to the core's normal behavior; no argument is needed for observation methods.

### reset

```ts
reset: () => Promise<void>;
```

### refresh

```ts
refresh: () => Promise<void>;
```

### clear

```ts
clear: () => void;
```

### setCoordinates

```ts
setCoordinates: ( transforms: CoordinateUpdate<E> | CoordinateUpdate<E>[], options?: ImmediatelyOptions & TransitionOptions ) => void;
```

### setState

```ts
setState: ( modifier: | CropperState | null | ((state: CropperState | null, settings: CropperSettings<E>) => CropperState | null), options?: TransitionOptions & ImmediatelyOptions & InteractionOptions & PostprocessOptions ) => void;
```

### setImage

```ts
setImage: (image: CropperImage) => void;
```

### flipImage

```ts
flipImage: (horizontal?: boolean | undefined, vertical?: boolean | undefined, options?: InteractionOptions & ImmediatelyOptions & NormalizeOptions & TransitionOptions) => void;
```

### zoomImage

```ts
zoomImage: (scale: Scale | number, options?: InteractionOptions & ImmediatelyOptions & NormalizeOptions & TransitionOptions) => void;
```

### rotateImage

```ts
